# Redefining Success Metrics

The concept that businesses and economies should measure success through broader indicators beyond GDP and financial growth.

## Core Argument
Relentless pursuit of profit has led to environmental degradation and widened social inequalities. Success metrics should incorporate social impact, employee well-being, environmental sustainability, and community outcomes.

## Alternative Models
- [[b-corporations]] as a framework for businesses prioritizing social impact
- Beyond GDP measurement approaches
- Employee well-being as a core business metric
- Environmental impact as a strategic consideration rather than externality

## Connection to Economic Thinking
Related to [[how-the-economic-machine-works---ray-dalio]] on how economic systems function and [[responsible-capitalism]] on rethinking the purpose of business.

